{"schema_version":1,"dataset":"synopsis_hub_diorama","adapter":"hub","trigger":"synopsis_hub_diorama","logical_grid":[480,270],"target_render":{"min_long_edge":1024,"scaling":"native_or_integer_nearest"},"generation_contract":{"images_per_job":1,"collage":false,"allow_flip":false,"allow_recolour_clone":false,"allow_smooth_upscale":false,"no_text":true,"no_ui":true},"enums":{"time_of_day":["dawn","day","golden_hour","civil_twilight","night"],"weather":["clear","overcast","rain","thunderstorm","snow","windy"],"season":["spring","summer","autumn","winter"],"split":["train","validation"]},"style_contract":{"pixel_scale":"fixed_logical_pixel_size","presentation":"nearest_neighbour","composition":"60/30/10","local_surface_shades":[3,5],"min_human_traces":3,"architecture":"compact practical one-to-two-storey scientific campus","forbidden":["giant ceremonial domes","palace colonnades","military styling","fantasy meteorology","mixed pixel scales","smooth antialiasing"]},"prompt_prefix":"Standalone single image, no frame, no text, no user interface, no collage. Original 26063 cozy scientific pixel-art language for a fictional educational and research meteorological campus of Northwestern Russia inspired by Petersburg scientific culture. Compose on a fixed logical 480x270 world grid: every logical pixel has one consistent display size, hard square pixel clusters, nearest-neighbour look, no anti-aliasing, no mixed pixel scales, no random single-pixel noise. Documentary plausibility, professional, cozy and lightly nostalgic rather than retro parody. Use the 60/30/10 composition rule: 60 percent calm large forms and breathing space, 30 percent functional architecture, instruments and vegetation, 10 percent accents. Use three to five shades per local material and include at least three believable human work traces when the scene allows. Meteorological maps and instruments remain scientifically precise and semantic weather colors must stay meaningful. For exterior views keep a low 